# rule.require.real-brain-tests-in-isolated-tempdir-and-home

a test that spawns a real brain-cli runs it in a `genTempDir` repo, with `HOME` = an isolated temp home
(`genIsolatedClaudeHome`, which links only the host credential), and every inherited `CLAUDE*` env var
dropped. never the host `~`, never the worktree as cwd.

why: the host's settings, trust, and CLAUDE.md are not the subject, and a real claude WRITES them
(trust, `/model`, "don't ask again"). a runner that is itself a claude leaks its session env into the
spawn (measured 2026-10-15: an inherited `CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION` turned transcripts off).

blocker: host `HOME` · non-temp cwd · inherited `CLAUDE*` env · a write to the host `~/.claude.json` or `~/.claude/`.
extant `*.realbrain.*` suites on the host home are fixed forward when touched.
